{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he appeared in the plains of Mamre.</b> Rashi explained: he is the one who gave him advice concerning circumcision. And it is perplexing: is a man as distinguished and righteous as Abraham, who was tested with ten trials and stood firm in all of them, and did not ask advice — how did he ask advice concerning circumcision that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him? One may say: heaven forbid that he asked advice whether to circumcise or not; rather, whether to do it privately or in public, and Mamre gave him advice to do it in public, so that people would see and circumcise after him. And that is what is written: בעצם היום הזה נימול אברהם — בעצומו של יום. Another explanation: he asked him advice from which place to circumcise, and he gave him advice to circumcise at the place of the male organ, as it is written: המול לכם כל זכר — from the place where male is distinguished from female. Another explanation: when the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him to circumcise all the men of his household, he went to Aner and Eshkol to ask what to do about the men of his household who did not want to be circumcised, and they did not know what to answer him. He went to Mamre, and he gave him advice: circumcise yourself and Ishmael your son first, and when they see this, they will then agree to be circumcised. And so he did: בעצם היום הזה נמול אברהם וישמעאל בנו, and then it is written: וכל אנשי ביתו נמלו אתו. And if you ask: Mamre, who gave him advice — why was he not circumcised in the end? He was circumcised at the end, as is stated in the Aggadah." "<b>Like the heat of the day.</b> The time of eating, which is the fourth hour, when the day began to get hot, and then every person eats. As Rav Pappa explained at the beginning of tractate Shabbat. And he stood at the entrance of the tent to see if any person would pass by at mealtime, and he would bring him into his house."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The note ends with a phrase beginning נמול כדאיתא באגדה; the implication is that Mamre was eventually circumcised, but the final clause is truncated or elliptical. Translated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:36.044633417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}